ID: Ch2-Stats
TEXT:

As we navigate the thick undergrowth, a series of sharp electronic chimes rings out from my right coat pocket.

"Barry, what is that chime?" Daren asks, glancing over his shoulder. "I know that sound. Don't tell me you hauled a fortune teller's trinket all the way to Varathia. Are you planning to read our palms, Barry?"

A fortune teller's trinket. That is what street peddlers call these devices. The underlying mechanics, however, are far more potent. The mechanism siphons ambient magical radiation from the surrounding atmosphere. In ordinary lands where mages are rare and rarely cast high-tier spells, the trickle-charge is negligible. But on Varathia, where hundreds of world-class mages unleash lethal sorcery in constant battle, the ambient mana density is immense.

I pull the device from my pocket. It looks like a compact metal slate fitted with small buttons and a luminous glass display. Characters flicker across the screen, categorizing numbers into 'stats'. The list includes physical enhancements—strength, speed, reflexes, toughness, observation, and hearing—alongside specialized disciplines like combat technique, ancient languages, and premonition.

Once enough ambient mana accumulates, the device chimes and unlocks an allotment of stat points. All values currently read zero; the merchant drained the charge completely before selling it.

Allocating points channels the stored mana directly through my aura, permanently reinforcing physical traits and sensory acuity. But every investment is final, and with no way to predict the next recharge cycle, each point demands careful calculation. The maximum cap for each attribute will likely expand as the device absorbs greater concentrations of power over time.

Fortune tellers prize the gadget for its premonition stat—vague flashes of incoming events they dress up as prophecy. The ancient languages category is what caught my eye. If it works as intended, it will translate archaic dialects and local inscriptions, invaluable on a continent where the common tongue cannot be taken for granted.

choice("Invest points now", Ch2-Stats-spent, v_current_scene = Ch2-Stats-spent, special:stats)
choice("Invest points later(by pressing the stats button on the top of the screen)", Ch2-Fallen-trees, v_current_scene = Ch2-Fallen-trees)


ID: Ch2-Stats-spent
TEXT:

