choice("Continue", Ch2-Fallen-trees, v_current_scene = Ch2-Fallen-trees)


ID: Ch2-Fallen-trees
TEXT:

"Barry, don't you think there are more pressing matters than tinkering with a toy?" Daren asks, glancing back at me.

"This isn't a toy," I reply, slipping the slate back into my coat. "And you might want to watch your footing instead of lecturing me. We just ran out of woods."

"Quiet, both of you. We have company," Kate hisses.

She is right. The forest ends abruptly at a wide clearing torn apart by violence. Shattered trunks and gouged earth litter the terrain, alongside a dozen contorted corpses. A fresh massacre. Three survivors are actively stripping the bodies, but our arrival brings them to a sudden halt.

All three turn to face us. The central figure is built like an ox—broad-shouldered, mid-forties, sporting a thick black beard that covers half his chest. He wears heavy iron plate and rests a massive double-bitted battleaxe across one shoulder. Flanking him are two leaner young men in chainmail vests, their hands empty.

The bearded man sneers at Daren across the field of corpses.

"Quite the company you keep, healer in armor. A healer, a banshee, and a baseline human. It's like you came here begging to die!"

The word banshee lands like a whip. Kate's jaw clenches, her gaze dropping to the dirt for a split second before her eyes harden into pure murder.

"Watch your tongue," I call out. "Who are you calling an ordinary human? Have you never heard of stillwaters?"

"Stillwaters are tavern fairy tales!" the bearded man barks with a laugh. "Whatever delusions brought you to Varathia, boy, you won't live to see sundown."

"Why?" Daren shouts, his voice thick with fury. "Why butcher these people?"

He sweeps an armored arm toward the dead scattered across the grass.

"No one ordered us to start slaughtering each other! The rules only stated that restrictions are lifted until the first objectives are issued! We don't even know if the trials demand bloodshed! Why murder them?"

"Because no rules means no consequences," the axe-wielder replies, his grin widening. "We're thinning the competition before the real games begin."

He rolls his shoulders, adjusting his grip on the axe haft.

"My boys and I were worried we might be out of our depth against world-class mages. But look at this! You bleed just like anyone else." He raises the axe high. "Enough chatter. You know what comes next."

#if(v_ch1_stillwater == 2) {
"Barry, get behind me!" Daren roars, stepping in front of me with sword drawn.
}
#if(v_ch1_stillwater == 1) {
His grin broadens, his eyes locking directly onto me.
}
"First rule of combat," the bearded man barks.

Space distorts. One of the young men beside him vanishes in a blur and snaps into existence directly behind me, a dagger gripped in reverse.

"Kill the weak first."

choice("Continue", Ch2-Battle-human, v_current_scene = Ch2-Battle-human, v_ch2_toughness_happened = 0) if (v_ch1_stillwater == 2)
choice("Continue", Ch2-Battle-stillwater, v_current_scene = Ch2-Battle-stillwater) if (v_ch1_stillwater == 1)


ID: Ch2-Battle-stillwater
TEXT:

set(v_ac_ch2_nails,1) if (v_premonition == 0 && v_reflexes == 0 && v_toughness > 2)
set(v_ch2_toughness_happened,0) if (v_premonition == 0 && v_reflexes > 0 || v_premonition == 0 && v_reflexes == 0 && v_toughness < 3 || v_premonition > 0)
set(v_ch2_toughness_happened,1) if (v_premonition == 0 && v_reflexes == 0 && v_toughness > 2)
achievement("Tough as nails",v_ac_ch2_nails)
#if(v_premonition > 0) {
The instant the young mage materializes at my back, a vivid flash seizes my mind: cold steel arcing straight for my throat. A premonition.

Trusting the flash, I drop my head and pivot. The blade whickers through empty air an inch above my collar. Before I can recover, the mage drives a heavy boot into my chest, knocking the wind out of me and slamming me flat onto the dirt.
}
#if(v_premonition == 0 && v_reflexes > 0) {
The young mage slashes his dagger toward my throat. My body reacts on pure reflex, ducking under the lethal sweep before my mind even registers the danger. The steel cuts empty air, but the mage instantly pivots and drives a heavy boot into my chest, sending me sprawling across the dirt.
}
#if(v_premonition == 0 && v_reflexes == 0 && v_toughness >= 3) {
The young mage slashes his dagger toward my throat. The strike is too fast for me to evade, but when the steel bites into my flesh, the reinforced skin holds like hardened leather. The blade scores a shallow red line without cutting deep. The mage stares at his dagger in disbelief, then drives a vicious boot into my chest, knocking me flat on my back.
}
#if(v_premonition > 0 || v_reflexes > 0 || v_toughness >= 3) {
"Barry!" Daren bellows, charging between me and my attacker and intercepting the follow-up strike with his heavy shield.

"Leaving the woman undefended? Rookie mistake!" the bearded man laughs.

His second son thrusts both hands forward. A dozen broadswords materialize out of thin air, hovering in a deadly fan before hurtling at Kate in a lethal barrage.

Frost erupts along Kate's left arm, instantly solidifying into a massive, heavy shield of sculptured ice. She slams it into position. The flying broadswords strike the frost barrier with deafening clangs, their tips embedded deep in the solid ice.

"Undefended?" Kate's voice cuts through the clearing, razor-sharp. "So which is it? A defenseless woman... or a banshee?"

She lowers the ice barrier, revealing eyes burning with cold fury.

"Make up your mind!" she roars, the force of her voice ringing through the silent woods.
}
#if(v_premonition == 0 && v_reflexes == 0 && v_toughness < 3) {
The young mage slashes his dagger toward my throat. The strike is too fast to dodge. Cold steel rips through my windpipe. I clamp both hands over the wound, but arterial blood surges through my fingers in hot, unstoppable pulses.

"Barry!" Daren screams across the clearing.

The world tilts. I catch a glimpse of Daren rushing toward me, white light flaring uselessly in his hands, before darkness pulls me under.
}

