ID: Ch2-Battle-human
TEXT:

The young mage slashes his dagger toward my throat, but Daren lunges forward, catching the blade against his steel shield with a deafening ring.

"Leaving the woman undefended? Rookie mistake!" the bearded man laughs.

His second son thrusts both hands forward. A dozen broadswords materialize out of thin air, hovering in a deadly fan before hurtling at Kate in a lethal barrage.

Frost erupts along Kate's left arm, instantly solidifying into a massive, heavy shield of sculptured ice. She slams it into position. The flying broadswords strike the frost barrier with deafening clangs, their tips embedded deep in the solid ice.

"Undefended?" Kate's voice cuts through the clearing, razor-sharp. "So which is it? A defenseless woman... or a banshee?"

She lowers the ice barrier, revealing eyes burning with cold fury.

"Make up your mind!" she roars, the force of her voice ringing through the silent woods.

choice("Continue", Ch2-Battle-begins, v_current_scene = Ch2-Battle-begins)


ID: Ch2-Battle-begins
TEXT:

The bearded man's arrogant grin vanishes. He takes half a step back, unsettled by the sheer weight of her presence. The killing intent radiating from Kate is suffocating.

"Backstabbers and sword-flingers," she says, her tone dropping to a lethal calm. "You call yourselves mages? Come. Let me show you real magic."

A biting chill sweeps the clearing, frosting the grass at our feet. This is what it means to stand among true elementalists.

The axe-wielder shakes off his hesitation with a furious snarl.

"Your parlor tricks won't save you a second time!" he roars. "Banshee or not, none of you leave this clearing alive!"

He charges Daren, raising his greataxe for a crushing blow.

Tactical reality hits me. If I stay pinned here, Daren will be forced to fend off both the brute and the teleporting flanker while keeping me alive. White-magic healing requires stillness and absolute focus—impossible in the chaos of a two-on-one melee. If Daren takes a bad hit, he won't be able to mend it.

I have to create an opening.

choice("Hide behind Daren and let him handle them both", Ch2-Hide, v_current_scene = Ch2-Hide)
choice("Draw the younger mage away from Daren and focus on avoiding his attacks", Ch2-Avoid, v_current_scene = Ch2-Avoid)
choice("Fight the younger mage myself", Ch2-Fight, v_current_scene = Ch2-Fight)


ID: Ch2-Hide
TEXT:

Jumping into the fray without a plan will only get in Daren's way. I stay back, tracking the movements across the clearing.

Kate has the sword-caster fully occupied. Broadswords rip through the air from every angle, only to shatter against solid slabs of ice she raises with flickers of her hands. It is an ideal matchup for us. Daren's armor cannot deflect high-tier enchanted weapons, and without magic of my own, airborne steel would butcher me in seconds.

The bearded man closes the distance. His greataxe crashes into Daren's raised broadsword with a concussive boom that shakes the dirt beneath our feet.

"Enchanted steel!" the brute grunts, leaning his massive weight into the bind. "Let's see how long you last against real muscle!"

He roars, forcing Daren's blade down. The teleporting son flashes into the flank, dagger aimed at my throat. Daren wrenches his shield across, taking the brunt of the strike on his rim while absorbing cuts along his armored shoulder.

"How long can you guard this dead weight?" the axe-wielder barks, swinging another heavy blow. "Drop the boy and fight!"

"Not a chance!" Daren snarls, parrying the heavy axe and driving a counter-thrust into the man's guard.

Across the field, the second son summons a ring of floating steel, surrounding Kate from all sides. He snaps his fingers; dozens of blades plunge inward in a synchronized execution. Kate encases herself in a solid sphere of opaque ice. Steel embeds harmlessly into the frost. She dispels the shell, and scores of blades clatter dead against the earth.

Beside me, the flanker keeps lunging. Daren parries every lethal cut meant for me, but the defense is costing him. Blood drips from gaps in his plate. He cannot hold a two-front fight much longer.

choice("Ask Kate for help", Ch2-Ask-Kate, v_current_scene = Ch2-Ask-Kate, v_ch2_kate_debt = 1)
choice("Draw the younger mage away from Daren and focus on avoiding his attacks", Ch2-Avoid, v_current_scene = Ch2-Avoid)
choice("Fight the younger mage myself", Ch2-Fight, v_current_scene = Ch2-Fight)


ID: Ch2-Avoid
TEXT:

Daren cannot hold two opponents while protecting me. Since the teleporting son wants my blood, I will draw him away and keep him chasing air until Daren drops the father.

Kate has the sword-caster fully occupied. Broadswords rip through the air from every angle, only to shatter against solid slabs of ice she raises with flickers of her hands. It is an ideal matchup for us. Daren's armor cannot deflect high-tier enchanted weapons, and without magic of my own, airborne steel would butcher me in seconds.

The bearded man closes the distance. His greataxe crashes into Daren's raised broadsword with a concussive boom that shakes the dirt beneath our feet.

"Enchanted steel!" the brute grunts, leaning his massive weight into the bind. "Let's see how long you last against real muscle!"

He roars, forcing Daren's blade down.

I break into a dead sprint toward the treeline. The flanker takes the bait, vanishing from Daren's side to pursue me.

"Barry, stay back!" Daren roars.

He tries to turn, but the greataxe forces him back into the guard. He cannot take his eyes off the brute for a fraction of a second.

Across the field, the second son summons a ring of floating steel, surrounding Kate from all sides. He snaps his fingers; dozens of blades plunge inward in a synchronized execution. Kate encases herself in a solid sphere of opaque ice. Steel embeds harmlessly into the frost. She dispels the shell, and scores of blades clatter dead against the earth.

choice("Continue", Ch2-Avoid2, v_current_scene = Ch2-Avoid2)


ID: Ch2-Avoid2
TEXT:

set(v_ac_ch2_nails,1) if (v_agility == 0 && v_ch2_toughness_happened == 0 && v_reflexes == 0 && v_toughness > 2)
achievement("Tough as nails",v_ac_ch2_nails)
#if(v_agility > 0) {
The sprint pays off instantly. The flanker blinks through space, reappearing directly in my path, but my boosted speed carries me clear before he can plant his feet. Every time he teleports to cut me off, I accelerate, pivoting past his lunges with ease. The stat booster's physical enhancement makes my stride effortless, burning ground without draining my stamina.
}
#if(v_agility == 0 && v_reflexes > 0) {
The evasion works better than I dared to hope. The flanker blinks through space, reappearing directly in my path, but my enhanced reflexes track the shift. Every time he slashes, I slip under the arc of the blade, weaving out of reach before he can recover his balance. The stat booster turns every near-miss into clean daylight.
}
#if(v_agility > 0 || v_reflexes > 0) {
"What are you doing?" the bearded man roars at his son. "Stop playing with your food and gut him! He's a baseline human!"

Kate seizes the offensive. She hurls jagged cones of ice in rapid succession, forcing the sword-caster to recall his floating blades to parry the projectiles. The moment he shifts to defense, she accelerates. Hundreds of needle-sharp ice daggers erupt from her aura in a freezing torrent. The volume of fire overwhelms him; a single misjudged deflection leaves his chest open, and an ice shard punches clean through his sternum, piercing his heart. He collapses into the mud.

"No!" the father screams, his head whipping toward his fallen son.

The distraction is fatal. Daren steps into the opening and drives his enchanted blade straight through the man's iron breastplate. The broadsword cuts steel and bone alike. The bearded man gurgles on blood, his grip slipping from the battleaxe before he hits the ground.

Panic takes the surviving flanker. He teleports toward the deep woods, but his range falls short, depositing him at the tree line. As he scrambles into the brush on foot, an ice spear hurled from Kate's palm drills through the back of his skull, dropping him dead in his tracks.

Silence crashes over the bloodstained clearing. My heart pounds against my ribs, hands trembling from the rush of surviving.
}
#if(v_agility == 0 && v_ch2_toughness_happened == 0 && v_reflexes == 0 && v_toughness >= 3) {
Luring the flanker away proves harder than planned. Without boosted speed, every teleport puts him right on my heels. Steel cuts closer with every strike. I need to get back to Daren before I run out of luck.

"Barry! Behind you!" Daren shouts.

Too late. The dagger sweeps across my throat before I can duck.

Cold steel bites into flesh, but reinforced skin stops the edge from cutting deep, yielding only a shallow scrape of blood. The attacker freezes, staring at his blade in utter confusion. I scramble backward out of reach, raising my guard for the next shift.

"What are you doing?" the bearded man roars at his son. "Stop playing with your food and gut him! He's a baseline human!"
}
#if(v_agility == 0 && v_ch2_toughness_happened == 1 && v_reflexes == 0) {
Luring the flanker away proves harder than planned. Without boosted speed, every teleport puts him right on my heels. Steel cuts closer with every strike. I need to get back to Daren before I run out of luck.

"Barry! Behind you!" Daren shouts.

Too late. The dagger sweeps across my throat before I can duck.

This time, the mage puts his entire weight behind the thrust, driving the blade through my hardened skin. Steel severs my carotid artery. I drop to my knees, clamping both hands over my throat, but hot blood pours through my fingers in heavy torrents.

"Barry!" Daren's scream echoes across the woods.

My vision blurs as the flanker raises his dagger for the final strike, and the world fades to black.
}
#if(v_agility == 0 && v_reflexes == 0 && v_toughness < 3) {
Luring the flanker away proves harder than planned. Without boosted speed, every teleport puts him right on my heels. Steel cuts closer with every strike. I need to get back to Daren before I run out of luck.

"Barry! Behind you!" Daren shouts.

Too late. The dagger sweeps across my throat before I can duck.

Cold steel slices clean through my windpipe. I collapse, clutching my neck as blood gushes over my hands.

"Barry!" Daren's scream echoes across the woods.

My vision blurs as the flanker raises his dagger for the final strike, and the world fades to black.
}
#if(v_agility == 0 && v_ch2_toughness_happened == 0 && v_reflexes == 0 && v_toughness > 2) {
Kate seizes the offensive. She hurls jagged cones of ice in rapid succession, forcing the sword-caster to recall his floating blades to parry the projectiles. The moment he shifts to defense, she accelerates. Hundreds of needle-sharp ice daggers erupt from her aura in a freezing torrent. The volume of fire overwhelms him; a single misjudged deflection leaves his chest open, and an ice shard punches clean through his sternum, piercing his heart. He collapses into the mud.

"No!" the father screams, his head whipping toward his fallen son.

The distraction is fatal. Daren steps into the opening and drives his enchanted blade straight through the man's iron breastplate. The broadsword cuts steel and bone alike. The bearded man gurgles on blood, his grip slipping from the battleaxe before he hits the ground.

Panic takes the surviving flanker. He teleports toward the deep woods, but his range falls short, depositing him at the tree line. As he scrambles into the brush on foot, an ice spear hurled from Kate's palm drills through the back of his skull, dropping him dead in his tracks.

Silence crashes over the bloodstained clearing. My heart pounds against my ribs, hands trembling from the rush of surviving.
}
choice("Continue", Ch2-Battle-end, v_current_scene = Ch2-Battle-end) if (v_agility == 0 && v_reflexes > 0 || v_agility == 0 && v_ch2_toughness_happened == 0 && v_reflexes == 0 && v_toughness > 2 || v_agility > 0)
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_agility == 0 && v_reflexes == 0 && v_toughness < 3 || v_agility == 0 && v_ch2_toughness_happened == 1 && v_reflexes == 0)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load) if (v_agility == 0 && v_reflexes == 0 && v_toughness < 3 || v_agility == 0 && v_ch2_toughness_happened == 1 && v_reflexes == 0)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves) if (v_agility == 0 && v_reflexes == 0 && v_toughness < 3 || v_agility == 0 && v_ch2_toughness_happened == 1 && v_reflexes == 0)


