ID: Ch2-Protection
TEXT:

achievement("An unlikely ally",v_ac_ch2_unlikely)
"Yes, I can," I tell her. "I overheard you talking about a cave. We are looking for shelter as well. We could offer you protection on your way back if you promise to let us share your cave for one night."

The doe measures me with large, dark eyes, ears flicking toward the distant rumbles of spellfire across the valley.

"We mean you no harm, I promise," I tell her, keeping my hands open and still.

"No," the doe says, tilting her head. "You don't. Otherwise I wouldn't still be standing here, having this conversation with you. I thank you, outlander. We accept your generous offer. My name is Elaria, and this is my child, Molan. I believe this is how humans make their acquaintance?"

She steps forward across the mossy shale and gracefully extends a slender front leg. Taking the offered hoof, I give it a brief, formal shake before letting go.

"I'm Barry," I tell her. "Pleased to meet you."

Beside me, Daren and Kate stare in utter bewilderment. To their ears, I just traded a series of strange clicks and bleats with a wild animal and concluded the negotiation with a handshake.

"Barry, what in the world?..." Daren asks, glancing from me to the doe with a furrowed brow.

"I'll explain later," I tell him. "They said they can lead us to their cave, in exchange for our protection. We're still looking for shelter, aren't we?"

"Well, I suppose, but..."

"Then come on, she says it's this way," I say, following the deer along the tree line.

Daren shakes his head in deep skepticism, but follows with hand on pommel. Kate watches with a raised brow, more intrigued than skeptical, as she falls into step behind us toward the rocky slopes.

choice("Next chapter", Ch3-Intro, v_next_chapter_crash = 1, v_current_scene = Ch3-Intro, v_chapter_save_counter = 5, v_checkpoint_rich = 1, special:checkpoint_save)


ID: Ch2-Travels
TEXT:

"Yes, I can," I tell her. "I just wanted to wish you safe travels."

"Oh..." she says, her ears perking up. "Thank you. I wish you safe travels as well, outlander. Come, my child, let us go."

As the two deer vanish into the thick mountain brush, Daren and Kate stare at me in dead silence.

"Barry, what in the world were you doing?" Daren asks, shaking his head. "Do you have any idea how ridiculous you sounded, whistling and clicking at a doe?"

"I'm sure I sounded absurd," I say, adjusting my pack. "Don't mind me, just letting off steam. Let's keep moving."

We head up the winding mountain path, scanning the rocky slopes in the hopes of finding a cave to shelter us for the night.

choice("Next chapter", Ch3-Intro, v_next_chapter_crash = 1, v_current_scene = Ch3-Intro, v_chapter_save_counter = 5, v_checkpoint_rich = 1, special:checkpoint_save)


ID: Ch2-Delicious
TEXT:

"Yes, I can," I tell her. "And if we starve on this mountain I make no promises."

"No! Stay away from us, monster. Child, quick, into the forest!" she cries, her hooves kicking up moss as both deer bolt into the thicket.

As the crashing in the brush fades, Daren and Kate stare at me in dead silence.

"Barry, what in the world were you doing?" Daren asks, shaking his head. "Do you have any idea how ridiculous you sounded, clicking and wheezing at a doe?"

"I'm sure I sounded absurd," I say, adjusting my pack. "Don't mind me, just letting off steam. Let's keep moving."

We head up the winding mountain path, scanning the rocky slopes in the hopes of finding a cave to shelter us for the night.

